# A Primer on Critical Race Theory.

**Authors:** Taylor, Edward

## Abstract
Describes critical race theory (CRT), an eclectic and dynamic form of legal scholarship that evolved as a response to the stalled progress of traditional civil rights litigation. CRT, as a form of oppositional scholarship, challenges the experience of whites as the normative standard and grounds its conceptual framework in the experiences of people of color. (SLD)

